      "notes": "The verdict is broadly well-constructed. The mixed/minor direction is justified: near-term cost of the fracking ban is genuinely minimal given the expert consensus on gas pricing and volumes; the coal-power ban formalises existing reality; the coking coal/steel uncertainty is real and correctly flagged. Job-creation claims are correctly labelled projected. The main issues are tier misclassifications on E3/E4/E5 \u2014 these are economic forecasts dressed as measurable facts \u2014 but they do not change the direction or magnitude of the verdict. No lever leakage, no party bias, no false balance detected. The 'mixed' verdict is justified by the genuine coking coal uncertainty on one side against minimal foregone gains on the other."
